*** Input file for program 'BPEident', 
*** for identification of material parameters of the Bart Peeters model
***
*1********************************************************
* Output filename string
sA9f                    OutID		(max. 4 characters; no extension)
*2********************************************************
* Filename for initial discretized texture [LINIX system = CaSe-SeNsItIvE]
DC06F250.SMT            TexID			(max. 12 characters including extension)
*3********************************************************
* Mechanical data (see comment #1)
i				MecDatTyp	
2     			iTotPaths		Number of subsequent strain paths 
s				PathType(i)		Type (of path nr. i) 
 -0.190                 AmDefo(i)	[/]	Amount of deformation (during pa
 90.00                  PathAng(i)	[°]	Angle (of path nr. i) from RD towards shear/tensile direction
s				PathType(i)		Type (of path nr. i) 
  0.8                   AmDefo(i)	[/]	Amount of deformation (during pa
 90.00                  PathAng(i)	[°]	Angle (of path nr. i) from RD towards shear/tensile direction
*4********************************************************
* Material constants
2.48E-10   			b	[m]	Magnitude of burgers vector
8.16E4      		G	[MPa]	Shear modulus
  0.20      		alpha	[/]	Dislocation interaction parameter
  0.20       		f	[/]	Volume fraction of CBBs (Cell Block Boundaries)
 53.0                   tau_0	[MPa]	Initial critical resolved shear stress on all slip systems
*5********************************************************
* Material parameters  === BPEmono_DC06 === BPEm_DC06 (19950020)
2.12E-2                 I	[/]	immobilization CBs
8.89E-10                R	[m]	recovery CBs
8.37E-1                 I_wd	[/]	immobilization CBBs
2.66E-8                 R_wd	[m]	recovery CBBs
2.27E-9                 R_ncg	[m]	recovery of old CBBs and polarity of old CBBs
9.59                    beta_1[/]	1st coeff. micro shear band cut-through of old CBBs
1.07                    beta_2[/]	2nd coeff. micro shear band cut-through of old CBBs
5.45E-2                 I_wp	[/]	immobilization polarity CBBs
1.44E-9                 R_wp	[m]	recovery polarity CBBs
4.12E-9                 R_rev	[m]	recovery of polarity CBBs during bauschinger
8.70E-9                 R_2	[m]	recovery of CBs due to reversal polarity flux
**********************************************************
comment #1:
-----------
In case MecDatTyp == 'i':
The deformation path is inputted within this file (in the lines following MecDatTyp), 
as in the following example:
i				MecDatTyp
1				iTotPaths		Number of subsequent strain paths 
	//1~monotonic test; more~Bauschinger or cross test
s				PathType(i)		Type (of path nr. i) 
	//'s'~simple shear test; 't'~uniaxial tensile test
  0.20			AmDefo(i)	[/]	Amount of deformation (during path nr. i) 
	//for PathType(i)=s: total shear (gamma) = tangent(total shear angle)
      //for PathType(i)=t: total true tensile strain epsilon_11
  0.00			PathAng(i)	[°]	Angle (of path nr. i) from RD to shear direction/tensile direction




	


